# survival_city.wmap -- SURVIVAL's telecrystals, in the WORLDMAP v1 contract (stdlib/worldmap/CONTRACT.md).
#
# The geometry is NOT here: SURVIVAL's CITY is generated by sv_city.prn (the C client's init_city_geo formulas). This file carries the
# part of the world that the contract owns and GoblinFoxDragon shares: the telecrystals. tools/sv_wmap_gen.py turns it into
# sv_crystal_data.prn (a generated table, like sp_map_data.prn); the cast rules themselves are stdlib/worldmap/wm_rules.prn, the same
# file the GFD server compiles to Go, so a crystal here and a crystal in GFD's town cannot disagree about rings, commit time,
# interruption or the travel-from-combat roll.
#
# Every crystal hops inside this one zone (SURVIVAL is a single level). cost is WOOD here (GFD charges gil: the server owns that
# column in GFD; offline SURVIVAL has no server, so the resource it has is the currency). All x/z are road intersections, clear of buildings.
#
#   crystal <id> <x> <z> <r> <dest_zone> <dx> <dz> <yaw_deg> <cost> <total_ms> <commit_ms> <prompt...>

worldmap 1
zone 5 field Survival_City
bound 1004

# the plaza hubs (the hero drops in at 0,0): one to each far corner of the 7 x 7
crystal SV_PLAZA_TO_NORTHEAST   -22 -48 10 5  690  690  225 3 1000 600 G: TELEPORT NORTHEAST
crystal SV_PLAZA_TO_SOUTHWEST    22 -48 10 5 -690 -690   45 3 1000 600 G: TELEPORT SOUTHWEST

# the far corners come home for free (GFD's MEADOW_RETURN row is free too), landing beside the hub's ring, never inside it
crystal SV_NORTHEAST_RETURN     710  710 10 5   -2  -70  180 0  900 500 G: RETURN TO THE PLAZA
crystal SV_SOUTHWEST_RETURN    -710 -710 10 5    2  -70  180 0  900 500 G: RETURN TO THE PLAZA
